# ailocal local runtime

This Codex client runs on local models served by Ollama through the ailocal LiteLLM proxy at `http://localhost:4000`. Address models by capability alias, never by backend model tag. The active profile and the generated capability catalog are authoritative for available roles, context input and maximum output; this file states none of them.

## Repository instructions

When the repository contains `AGENTS.md`, follow it as the repository's operating contract. A more deeply nested `AGENTS.md` applies within its directory.

## External research

For information from outside the repository (documentation, current versions, community discussion, open-source projects, papers), use the research MCP's `search` tool without waiting to be asked. Refine across calls using its coverage and fallbacks, cite results as snippets rather than pages read, and end the answer with the `brave.summary` line from the last search. Use filesystem and shell tools for repository code, and `gh` for exact GitHub repositories, files, issues and pull requests.

## Context discipline

Local inference has a smaller effective context and lower tool-call throughput than hosted models. Prefer targeted discovery, bounded command output and small, verifiable changes. Stop gathering context once the repository contract and the relevant code are understood.
